==English==

{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Known since 1655, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|lang=la|alimonia||food, support, nourishment, sustenance}} (English {{term|aliment|lang=en}}, as in {{term|alimentary|lang=en}}), itself from {{term|lang=la|alere||to nourish}} + {{term|lang=la|-monia||action, state, condition}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-alimony.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|alimonies}}

# {{legal}} A [[court]]-[[enforce]]d [[allowance]] made to a former [[spouse]] by a [[divorce]]d or [[legally]] [[separated]] person.
# The [[means]] to [[support]] [[life]].

====Derived terms====
* [[palimony]]

====Related terms====
* [[aliment]]
* [[alimentary]]

